  "note": "Three get-all replies from the diagnostics download @sciurius attached to issue #681 on 2026-11-05, recorded while he kept two schedule tasks in the app (task 1: a charge task 07:00-08:00 from solar and grid at 2500 W with a 95 % SoC target; task 2: a Solar only charge task 08:00-10:00) and switched task 2 off and on again in the app. In the first frame task 2 is off, in the second it is on again, and the third was read right after the off write and still shows it on: the first readback after an app write is stale, the new state shows within about two minutes. Task 1 stays on in all three. Frames are in that order, not by time. Timestamps are UTC; his clock runs one hour ahead. The download was masked before upload and every frame here passes the integration's own masking unchanged. The fixture also holds the app's two writes of that toggle (task 2 off, then on; each carries the whole list of both tasks) and the device's acknowledgement of each. The writes carry Solar only as source 0 with an explicit 0 W, the acknowledgements leave both zeros out.",
